{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1252654-the-wild-corners-of-old-arcadia","id":1252654,"title":"The Wild Corners of Old Arcadia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-08T20:32:37-07:00","id":1252654,"title":"The Wild Corners of Old Arcadia","content":"In the Oneiromancy section of 2e is this very interesting tidbit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The edges of a Dreaming Road are unusual opportunities for the Storyteller to introduce crossovers into realms associated with other game lines, anywhere that an unrestrained dream path might intrude. Some potential destinations include the wild corners of Old Arcadia, where the Fae have no purchase. </div> </div> </div> Am I reading this right as a reference to Mage Arcadia, or is it pointing to something else in CofD I might have missed?<br /> <br /> As you may know Mage developer <span style=\"color:#000000\">Dave Brookshaw clarified in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=813206#post813206\">this post</a> that his interpretation of Mage Arcadia has absolutely no connection to Changeling Arcadia, going as far as saying that &quot;for now, Mage is written from the hard angle that Changeling The Lost doesn't exist&quot;. As a player, this feels like an extremely inelegant solution to the issue of having two game lines within the same universe awkwardly sharing the terminology &quot;Arcadia&quot; and &quot;Fae&quot; for completely separate things, and then just brushing it under the rug by one game ignoring the other's existence. That being said, I get it's a tough dilemma to solve since M:TAw 1e was in all likelihood written way before C:TL's core concept was even being discussed.</span><br /> <br /> I really do like the solution Changeling 2e seems to be offering however, if I understand correctly what's being implied here: that C:TL's True Fae are exiles from an older Arcadia, exiles who then recreated a new Arcadia on land stolen from the verderers. I love the depths this kind of obscure, distant mythology would add to Changeling's lore, and how it would link it with Mage harmoniously, but am I reading way too much into it or was this indeed the authors' intention?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T20:43:27-07:00","id":1252658,"title":"","content":"Old Arcadia is the realm of the Huntsman, not Supernal Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Supernal Arcadia isn't even a place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T20:52:06-07:00","id":1252659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1252654-the-wild-corners-of-old-arcadia?p=1252658#post1252658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Old Arcadia is the realm of the Huntsman, not Supernal Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, interesting, so that would mean the Dreaming Road would lead the characters back in time to Arcadia before the Gentry came in?<br /> <br /> But then I'm confused why they'd write it in the crossover paragraph as a one of the &quot;realms associated with other game lines&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T21:43:52-07:00","id":1252664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BetterWorldz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1252654-the-wild-corners-of-old-arcadia?p=1252659#post1252659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, interesting, so that would mean the Dreaming Road would lead the characters back in time to Arcadia before the Gentry came in?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> The Gentry go to a place in Arcadia that is not their domain when they wish to send a Huntsman after a changeling. It's got the hallmarks of a place out of time, such that the notion of needing time travel to get there is not so much unthinkable as irrelevant \u2014 the woods have always been there, and they'll always be there, regardless of whether the Strangers rule the roost in the new Arcadia of might and magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But then I'm confused why they'd write it in the crossover paragraph as a one of the &quot;realms associated with other game lines&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Not one page earlier the book uses the phrase &quot;old Arcadia&quot; in the main body of text in a paragraph theorizing why Hedgespinning doesn't work on the Dreaming Roads. The phrase &quot;the corners of Arcadia&quot; shows up in the first paragraph of the book's section on Huntsmen in reference to the places they are found, which escaping changelings sometimes stumble through on their way out.<br /> <br /> It presumably mentions it first because it's the <i>least cosmologically distant</i> of the things in that section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T22:18:11-07:00","id":1252669,"title":"","content":"Thanks, you're right I misinterpreted. &quot;Old Arcadia&quot; is also mentioned as the home of the Huntsmen in their Aspirations paragraph.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1252654-the-wild-corners-of-old-arcadia?p=1252664#post1252664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It presumably mentions it first because it's the <i>least cosmologically distant</i> of the things in that section.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I suppose that makes sense. Guess I got overly excited seing Arcadia referenced in that crossover-y context.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T04:12:33-07:00","id":1252713,"title":"","content":"Just to confirm, no, that line has nothing to do with Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}